WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768
-We've talked a lot on the show
about "Second Chance Theater,"

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
sketches that -- that,
like, killed at the table...

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and then died
in front of the audience.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right, right.
-You had the reverse happen.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Which, if you --

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:09.843 line:92%
which is very hard to do.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.811
I don't quite understand how --
how did you get a sketch on

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:12.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
that didn't have to go
to the table?

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:17.083
-This was an incredible moment.
I-I'm pretty sure this happened.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:17.851 line:92%
I don't remember everything.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a very long time ago.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
But "The Herlihy Boy."
-Yeah.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, so what happened was,
I was starting to --

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.160
like, people were starting
to like some of the stuff I did.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.563
And Lorne --
I wasn't on the show that week.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.898 line:92%
And Lorne said to Jim Downey,

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Adam's light.
Ask him if he has anything."

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- And so after the --
you know,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.670 line:92%
usually, you've got to read

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.973
in front of the whole cast
and -- and the whole crew.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if they laugh and --
you get it on.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:43.309 size:88% position:44% line:92%
If they don't, you know,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a lot of times,
my stuff didn't work.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:48.448
But this, "The Herlihy Boy" --
somehow, I was asked to be on.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:52.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wrote it, like, late on
a Wednesday night and did it.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was
the sneakiest thing ever.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.390
-And for those who don't
remember "The Herlihy Boy,"

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
definitely go on YouTube
and look it up.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's -- Yeah.
-I mean, in the end, you know,

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.665
you really -- it's really
a sketch about Farley.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was the --
-You're "The Herlihy Boy."

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Right.
-But you definitely --

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
you handed the best stuff off,
yeah.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had the title role.
But I knew the man.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:17.143
The man -- that -- that was
a big move, man, in my era.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.378 line:92%
If you wrote Farley into a skit,

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
you knew it was probably
gonna get on.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was probably gonna be
a great time.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.516 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-You guys, this was --

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.251
growing up,
I remember watching this sketch

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
and enjoying "The Gap Girls"
a great deal.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure. Yeah. That was fun.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:32.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was it as much --
-That was fun, yeah.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-That was Spade.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
Spade used to write those.
-Spade wrote those?

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
We had --

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.466
We had a great time doing that.
I used to -- I don't know.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
Me and Farley didn't look
as good as Spade.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
Spade kind of fit that stuff
better than us.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Spade
does kind of look...

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Spade has a nice
little body on him, and...

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...me and Farley
are a little bigger -- bigger.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
We didn't make sense
in the outfits.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Spade kept it,
because I remember

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
when Spade came back
and hosted in my era, he --

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.316
I think he played Martha Stewart
right away.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right, right, right.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he's managed
to maintain that, yeah.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
The -- The thing about Spade
in "Gap Girls"

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
is he's just talking
with his voice.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.960 size:75% position:38%
-No -- Everyone else
would put on, like,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:07.994 line:92%
a little higher, weird things.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's just like,
"Hey, what's up, everybody?"

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.598 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.466
-When we get back, I want
to talk about the special.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
But one of the things
I want to say is, you know,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think this is true
of your work over your career

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
and why people care about you
so much and your work

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it's really funny,
but it's also really sweet.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:29.082
And you had -- you sort of chose
to -- to do a song about Farley

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the special.
-Yeah, yes. Yes.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:34.320
-And it seemed like such a thing
that everybody wanted to hear.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.889
Was it --
When you first started doing it,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.724
obviously, when you were working
on your special...

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...was it nice to know

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
that everybody still wants
to connect to Farley that way?

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:41.594 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh. Oh, yeah, man.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sang -- I remember the first
couple of times I sang it.

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:48.234
And it was a nice electric
feeling in the audience.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everybody loved Farley
so much.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
And any time I said his name,
people would cheer.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was great.

